The Constitution text is copied from the website of the Legislation and Legal Opinion Commission,
Kingdom of Bahrain (https://www.lloc.gov.bh), page "The Constitution of the Kingdom of Bahrain", last
updated 25-April-2025. The Commission marks the English as an unofficial translation.

Basis for reuse. Legislative Decree (Law) No. 22 of 2006 on the Protection of Copyright and
Neighbouring Rights, Article 4(2), says protection shall not include:

  "Statutes, court judgments, arbitrators' awards, resolutions issued by administrative committees
  that enjoy judicial jurisdiction, international agreements and all official documents as well as
  the official translations of any of the above."

The site's own terms (https://www.lloc.gov.bh/en/page/Terms-and-Conditions) say its contents "are
protected by copyright" and may not be used "for any other purpose" without permission. Both are
recorded here; the text is published only under the Article 4(2) exemption, and will be withdrawn on
request.

The "legal-system" facts come from Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), released under CC0 1.0.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
